# answer/pi/form-markdown 160x45 @0,25 (160x15)
╭─ 1 of 1  ○ Q1 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Should the endpoint send one JSON response with a kind field, and send redirects as a 200 response body that page.tsx acts on?                               │
│                                                                                                                                                              │
│ ›1 ○ A. A 200 response like {kind: "redirect", location, permanent}. page.tsx calls permanentRedirect() (308) or redirect(). The redirect is cached per URL  │
│      like any other result. (recommended)                                                                                                                    │
│  2 ○ B. Django answers with a real 301, and the Next.js fetch reads the Location header: simpler for legacy callers, as the RFC has it.                      │
│    The CmsPageModal keeps reading Location, and nothing in the legacy code changes.                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                              │
│  3 ○ Write your own answer                                                                                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                              │
│ Recommended: A. The redirect stays inside the cached result, and the legacy CmsPageModal can simply ignore that kind.                                        │
│                                                                                                                                                              │
